  "summary": {
    "plain": "After 13 months of data, XENON100 saw two candidate events, consistent with the expected background, and no dark matter.",
    "technical": "224.6 live days x 34 kg; two candidates in 6.6-30.5 keVnr against 1.0 +/- 0.2 expected background events; profile likelihood limit on spin-independent elastic WIMP-nucleon scattering with a minimum of 2e-45 cm^2 at 55 GeV/c^2 (90% CL), the most stringent for WIMP masses above 8 GeV/c^2 according to the abstract."
  },
